    <a class="card" href="building-agents/development-workflow/tui/overview" style="text-decoration:none;color:inherit;">
      <h3>Chat in your terminal</h3>
      <p>Streaming responses, slash commands for release and deploy workflows, plus an on-host TUI that runs inside the container.</p>
    </a>
  </div>

  <h2>How Cast is organized</h2>
  <p>The docs are split into three top-level categories:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Getting Started</strong> — install, quick start, concepts, and the global Cast settings file.</li>
    <li><strong>Building Agents</strong> — create / edit / run agents; the development workflow (TUI, sessions, walkthrough); versioning (undo log + Git); and deployment (releases, lifecycle, providers).</li>
    <li><strong>Configuration</strong> — per-agent settings: custom tools, MCP servers, and persistent memory.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Reference is auto-generated where it should be and hand-written where it matters.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Reference</strong> — every <code>cast &lt;command&gt;</code> and <code>/slash-command</code> is extracted from the source on every build.</li>
    <li><strong>Prose</strong> — concept pages, walkthroughs, and deployment deep-dives are written by humans and linked from the reference.</li>
    <li><strong>Status</strong> — see when the reference was last extracted, what's new in the manifest, and which commands still need a prose page.</li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
